WEBVTT

00:00.238 --> 00:03.085
- We're to let a and
b be rational numbers,

00:03.085 --> 00:05.828
and let b be non-zero, they
have to say let b be non-zero

00:05.828 --> 00:08.002
because we're about to divide by b.

00:08.002 --> 00:11.853
Is a over b rational or irrational?

00:11.853 --> 00:13.531
Well let's think about it,
they're both rational numbers

00:13.531 --> 00:16.314
so that means that a, since
it's rational, can be expressed

00:16.314 --> 00:19.971
as the ratio of two integers,
so I can write a is equal to m

00:19.971 --> 00:24.116
over n, and same thing about
b, I could write b as being

00:24.116 --> 00:28.999
equal to p over q, where

00:28.999 --> 00:33.035
where m, n, p,

00:33.035 --> 00:36.419
and q are integers,

00:36.419 --> 00:39.832
are integers, by definition of what a

00:39.832 --> 00:41.478
rational number is, they're
telling us these numbers

00:41.478 --> 00:44.363
are rational so I can express
them as these types of ratios.

00:44.363 --> 00:46.528
So what is a over b going to be?

00:46.528 --> 00:48.800
a over b is going to be

00:48.800 --> 00:53.800
m over n over p over q

00:54.044 --> 00:57.822
which is equal to m over n,
if I divide by a fraction,

00:57.822 --> 01:00.382
it's the same thing as
multiplying by the reciprocal.

01:00.382 --> 01:04.017
q over p, let me write that a little bit,

01:04.017 --> 01:07.317
q over p which is equal to

01:07.317 --> 01:10.811
mq over np.

01:10.811 --> 01:13.128
Well mq is going to be an
integer, if the product of

01:13.128 --> 01:15.809
two integers is going to be
an integer, and np is going

01:15.809 --> 01:17.597
to be another integer, the
product of two integers

01:17.597 --> 01:20.558
is an integer, so I've just shown that

01:20.558 --> 01:22.935
a over b can be

01:22.935 --> 01:25.516
expressed as the ratio of
two integers, so a over b

01:25.516 --> 01:28.827
is for sure, in fact I've just
proven it to you, a over b

01:28.827 --> 01:32.231
is for sure going to be rational.

01:32.231 --> 01:35.129
Let's do a few more of
these, this is interesting.

01:35.129 --> 01:38.785
All right, so now we're saying let a and b

01:38.785 --> 01:41.224
be irrational numbers.

01:41.224 --> 01:45.449
Is a over b, let a and
b be irrational numbers.

01:45.449 --> 01:48.761
Is a over b rational or irrational?

01:48.761 --> 01:50.914
And, like always, pause
the video and try to think

01:50.914 --> 01:53.658
this through, and you
might want do some examples

01:53.658 --> 01:56.095
of some irrational numbers
and see if you can get,

01:56.095 --> 01:57.498
when you divide them, you can get rational

01:57.498 --> 01:59.631
or irrational numbers.

01:59.631 --> 02:01.845
Well, let's just imagine
a world where, let's say,

02:01.845 --> 02:04.848
that a is equal to, I dunno,

02:04.848 --> 02:07.103
two square roots of two,

02:07.103 --> 02:10.760
and b is equal to the square root of two.

02:10.760 --> 02:14.294
Well, in that world, a
over b, a over b would be

02:14.294 --> 02:18.103
two square roots of two
over the square root of two

02:18.103 --> 02:20.975
which would be two, which is
very much a rational number,

02:20.975 --> 02:23.027
I can express that as a ratio
of integers, I can write that

02:23.027 --> 02:25.851
as two over one, there's actually
an infinite number of ways

02:25.851 --> 02:28.089
I can express that as a
ratio of two integers.

02:28.089 --> 02:32.112
So, in this case, I was able
to get a over b to be rational,

02:32.112 --> 02:34.408
based on a and b being irrational.

02:34.408 --> 02:37.764
But, what if, what if instead of,

02:37.764 --> 02:39.938
what if a was equal to

02:39.938 --> 02:41.520
the square root of two

02:41.520 --> 02:45.482
and b is equal to the square root

02:45.482 --> 02:50.482
of, let's say, b is equal
to the square root of seven.

02:50.561 --> 02:54.190
Well, then a over b would
be equal to the square root

02:54.190 --> 02:57.704
of two over the square root
of seven, which is still

02:57.704 --> 03:00.204
going to be irrational, I
mean another way to think

03:00.204 --> 03:02.377
about it, and I'm not proving
it here, but you could

03:02.377 --> 03:03.962
think about it, this is
going to be the square root

03:03.962 --> 03:07.427
of two sevens, so we
have something that's not

03:07.427 --> 03:10.243
a perfect square under the
radical, so we're going

03:10.243 --> 03:13.574
to end up with an irrational number.

03:13.574 --> 03:16.338
So, we can show one example where a over b

03:16.338 --> 03:18.796
is rational and we showed one example

03:18.796 --> 03:23.084
where it is irrational,
so it can be either way.

03:24.094 --> 03:26.544
Let's do a few more of these.

03:26.544 --> 03:30.323
All right, let a be a
non-zero rational number.

03:30.323 --> 03:33.757
Is a times the square root of
eight rational or irrational?

03:33.757 --> 03:38.043
Well, the key here is, if you
multiply an irrational number

03:38.043 --> 03:40.461
and why is this an irrational number?

03:40.461 --> 03:42.818
It has a perfect square
in it, but it's not

03:42.818 --> 03:44.707
a perfect square in and of itself.

03:44.707 --> 03:47.165
The square root of eight is,
the square root of eight is

03:47.165 --> 03:50.376
equal to the square
root of four times two,

03:50.376 --> 03:52.467
which is equal to the
square root of four times

03:52.467 --> 03:54.500
the square root of two, which is equal

03:54.500 --> 03:56.755
to two square roots of two.

03:56.755 --> 03:58.950
And, this is kind of
getting to the punchline

03:58.950 --> 04:02.566
of this problem, but if I
multiply a rational times

04:02.566 --> 04:05.918
an irrational, I am going
to get an irrational.

04:05.918 --> 04:07.909
So the square root of
eight is an irrational,

04:07.909 --> 04:11.973
and if I multiply that
times a rational number,

04:11.973 --> 04:16.107
I'm still going to get
an irrational number.

04:16.107 --> 04:19.989
So this is going to be,
for sure, irrational.

04:19.989 --> 04:22.642
Let's do one more of these.

04:22.642 --> 04:25.437
So we're to let a be an irrational number.

04:25.437 --> 04:29.296
Is negative 24 plus a
rational or irrational?

04:29.296 --> 04:32.771
And I won't give a formal
proof here, but to give you

04:32.771 --> 04:35.047
more of an intuitive feel,
it's nice to just try out

04:35.047 --> 04:37.017
some numbers, and I encourage
you to pause the video

04:37.017 --> 04:39.513
and try to think through it yourself.

04:39.513 --> 04:44.372
Let's just imagine some values,
imagine if a is irrational,

04:44.372 --> 04:48.977
a is irrational, so what
if a was equal to negative

04:48.977 --> 04:52.128
pi, which is approximately
equal to negative three point

04:52.128 --> 04:54.911
one four one five nine and it keeps going

04:54.911 --> 04:59.123
on and on forever, never repeating.

04:59.123 --> 05:02.468
Well, then we would have

05:02.468 --> 05:05.528
negative 24 plus a

05:05.528 --> 05:09.780
would be equal to negative 24 minus pi,

05:09.780 --> 05:12.539
which would be approximately negative 27

05:12.539 --> 05:15.979
point one for one five
nine, the decimal expansion,

05:15.979 --> 05:17.535
everything to the right of
the decimal, is going to be

05:17.535 --> 05:19.931
the exact same thing as pi.

05:19.931 --> 05:22.186
So this looks like, at least
for this example, is going

05:22.186 --> 05:25.620
to be irrational, and let's
see, if a was square root of two

05:25.620 --> 05:29.595
negative 24 plus the square root of two,

05:29.595 --> 05:32.855
well, once again, I'm
not doing a proof here,

05:32.855 --> 05:36.766
but intuitively, this is
going to be a decimal,

05:36.766 --> 05:38.459
it's going to have a decimal expansion

05:38.459 --> 05:40.836
that's going to go on
forever and never repeat,

05:40.836 --> 05:43.294
and so this would just
change what's to the left

05:43.294 --> 05:46.382
of the decimal, but not
really change what's,

05:46.382 --> 05:48.507
well it would change what's
to the right of the decimal

05:48.507 --> 05:50.681
because this is negative,
but it's still going to go on

05:50.681 --> 05:54.906
forever and never repeat,
and if, in fact, this was

05:54.906 --> 05:58.132
if this was this way, then
to the right of the decimal,

05:58.132 --> 06:00.326
you would have the same thing
as the square root of two

06:00.326 --> 06:02.012
to the left of the decimal,
you would just have

06:02.012 --> 06:05.974
a different value, you
would have negative 25 point

06:05.974 --> 06:09.306
whatever whatever whatever,
and so this is, when you add

06:09.306 --> 06:13.431
a rational number to an
irrational number, we've proven

06:13.431 --> 06:16.661
in other videos, a
rational plus an irrational

06:16.661 --> 06:20.217
is going to be irrational, irrational.

06:20.217 --> 06:22.269
If you want that proof,
we have other videos

06:22.269 --> 06:24.774
within this tutorial.
